gambatte-pico patch to upstream gambatte (libgambatte/src/gambatte.cpp), GPL-2.0 like the file it
changes. Copyright (c) 2026 TheGammaSqueeze. Applied by build.sh to a copy in out/src.

A save state was gathered in a structure left as the stack had it, and only the fields the running
cartridge and machine use are written: an MBC-less cartridge (Dr. Mario) never sets the RAM bank
mode, so that byte of the state was the stack's leftovers. Two consoles saving the same machine got
different bytes whenever their stacks differed (one had its in-game menu open), and the netplay
check saw them part although the games were identical. The structure is now zeroed first, which
covers every such field (0003 cleared one of them by hand).

--- a/libgambatte/src/gambatte.cpp	2026-11-24 09:46:42.959564713 +0000
+++ b/libgambatte/src/gambatte.cpp	2026-11-24 09:46:42.977164712 +0000
@@ -155,7 +155,9 @@
 }
 
 void GB::saveState(void *data) {
-   SaveState state;
+   /* zeroed first: what the cartridge, the sound or the video leave unwritten (an MBC-less
+    * cartridge has no RAM bank mode) is 0, not the stack's leftovers */
+   SaveState state = SaveState();
    p_->cpu.setStatePtrs(state);
    p_->cpu.saveState(state);
    StateSaver::saveState(state, data);
